you wanted to be apart of our next big thing , this is it cyhd

cyberhand technologies international has revolutionary products that can save countless millions in unnecessary medical claims

news : up to 70 % of all work - related injury claims can be attributed to repetitive stress injuries , with the majority of those coming from carpal tunnel syndrome .

these injuries cost employers , insurance companies and individuals over $ 2 billion dollars a year in lost wages , lost productivity and paid worker ' s comp and insurance claims . not only are they a major cost to nearly every large corporation , the can be devastating to small companies , the self - employed and even individuals that are not even in the workforce .

while more and more people finally seem to realize the enormous scope of this problem , few are doing much to help resolve it . how can we get to the root of the problem the flawed ergonomics that caused millions of people and employers to suffer needlessly ?

finally , a real solution

cyberhand technologies international has been quietly developing multiple lines of products that go right to the heart of this multi - billion dollar epidemic workplace and online gaming ergonomics . cyberhand has tapped some of the world ' s leading workplace scientists , k inesiologists and engineers to design its unique , patent protected products that enable people to work and play much more effectively and efficiently with computers , pda ' s , smart - phones and video games , without the devastating repetitive stress injuries that so often accompany long hours in front of a computer or mobile computing device .

why is this so important ?

because when any company has the potential to save other companies millions or even billions of dollars , you can count on one sure thing they will get noticed !

cyberhand ' s market potential is huge

the markets that cyberhand is entering are measured in the billions of dollars . the u . s . market alone for its first ergonomic computer mouse offering is estimated at over $ 500 million . even if cyberhand is able to capture only a few percent of this market right away , sales from its unique computer mice could be anywhere from $ 10 to $ 25 million .

the computer gaming peripherals market is estimated to be worth $ 6 billion dollars in the u . s . alone and is and growing at an amazing 34 % year over year . if it was only able to secure a very small fraction of this marketplace , cyberhand could realize tens of millions of dollars in new revenues over the next few years .

the pda or handheld market is equally impressive , experiencing an annual global growth rate of 38 % . the market is projected to be a $ 35 billion market in 2006 and that does not even include the cellular or smart - phone peripheral market when cyberhand is also introducing revolutionary products .

this is big business ! ! !

addressing the root cause of repetitive stress injuries is and will continue to be a rapidly growing a multi - billion dollar business . since the advent of distributed computing in the 1980 ' s , the world ' s economy has come to rely heavily on personal computers ( pcs ) and workstations . in just a couple of decades , the pc with its ever increasing capability to dramatically increasing human productivity and entertain , has evolved from a novelty into an indispensable fixture in seemingly nearly every home and business in the developed world .

still , the injuries its repeated uses cause have been brushed aside for years , even as the hard costs associated with them rocket into the stratosphere .

how big is this problem ?

the national occupational research agenda ( nora ) and musculoskeletal di sorders and health administration ( osha ) report that based on information provided by the u . s . bureau of labour statistics in 2001 in the us alone , more than $ 2 . 1 billion in workers ' compensation costs and $ 90 million in indirect costs ( hiring , training , overtime , and administrative costs ) are incurred annually for these msd ( musculoskeletal disorders ) . in 1994 , 332 , 000 msd cases due to rsi were reported in u . s . workplaces . this figure represents nearly 65 % of all illness cases reported to the u . s . bureau of labour statistics . and , these numbers are increasing by an average of more than 10 % a year . the cost is staggering !

7 . 5 million workdays a year lost to carpal tunnel syndrome injuries !

the most frequently reported upper - extremity msd cases affect the hand / wrist region , with carpal tunnel syndrome ( cts ) being the most widely recognized condition . work - related cts injuries typically require an average of 30 lost workdays per injured worker . in 2000 alone ( the last year of reported statistics ) there were 250 , 000 reported cases . that is 7 . 5 million lost workdays !

what is being done to curb this billion dollar problem ?

cyberhand technologies international is quickly emerging as a leader in this huge market . cyberhand has developed three distinct , patent - protected lines of products that directly counter the most common causes of repetitive stress injuries .

the company ' s initial ground breaking product offering include :

an ergonomic computer mouse product line that eliminates computer related repetitive stress injuries ;

wireless keyboards for personal di gital assistants ( pdas ) and smart - phones currently sold under the pocketop brand ;

computer game controllers that are 40 % more responsive then its competitor ' s products .

cyberhand also offers software and accessories that compliment and extend the functionality of the company ' s devices .

cyberhand ' s products , with their innovative ergonomic designs and leading edge technologies that are superior to other products already on the market , could quickly become the gold standard in this multi - billion dollar market segment . this company could go from early stage to a $ 100 + blockbuster almost overnight . not only is that good news for cyberhand , it could be even better news for investors that are savvy enough to scoop the company ' s stock up at ground floor prices .

demand for cyberhand ' s products is expected to be phenomenal

major retailers and wholesalers , as well as some of the world ' s largest corporations , have already indicated that they are prepared to purchase or stock cyberhand ' s products in the tens or even hundreds of thousands right away . they have the foresight to see how big this can be . do you ?

in addition , cyberhand has 10 products in either the prototype or design stage . this means that the company should continue to release a constant stream of highly sought after products for years to come as its name recognition and credibility as a leader in its industry continues to grow .

all intellectual property and recent product upgrades ( fully patent protected ) have been developed in - house with turnaround time substantially less than any other competitor in the industry . this allows cyberhand to go from whiteboard to production in as little as ninety days with a complete prototype evolution .

two kinds of growth should mean higher revenues and faster growth

cyberhand ' s business - savvy executives are not satisfied with just the phenomenal growth estimates they believe will come from their own internally - developed product lines . they have undertaken a very aggressive acquisition strategy wherein cyberhand is actively seeking out other companies with cutting - edge technology and products that compliment cyberhand ' s products and negotiating to acquire these companies .

the company ' s first major acquisition was pocketop computer corporation , a privately held company that helped pioneer innovations in the portable handheld market in an effort to propel users into the next era of mobile computing . pocketop has developed a new product that we believe is expected to become the defacto standard in the pda portable keyboard market .

this gigantic handheld device marketplace ( one of the fastest growing consumer electronics markets ) is one of cyberhand ' s main areas of focus and the acquisition of pocketop has helped cyberhand jump right to the forefront of the market .

better yet , cyberhand shows no signs of slowing down . the company has indicated that it is currently evaluating several other potential acquisition candidates and could be getting close to closing its next deal . the story just keeps getting better .

